      "writtenOn": "2018-02-21T23:45:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not a big fan of this. It does 2 things that I\u0027d like to avoid:\n1) the implementation details of SignalStrength are on display here with the \"if (thresholds[0] \u003d\u003d 255) {use alternate behavior}\" thing.\n2) by not specifying meaningful defaults anywhere, any manufacturer that wishes to use RSCP must supply their own values. We should come up with reasonable defaults and have a way to use them so that by default they are consistent across the ecosystem.\n\nThings we could do:\n1) specify meaningful defaults in CC and use RSCP by default if it\u0027s available; or\n2) put meaningful defaults in SignalStrength.java and allow this key to be optional.\n\nWe could also:\n\n3) add an additional CC to say what reported quantity should be used such as (KEY_WCDMA_DEFAULT_SIGNAL_STRENGTH_MEASUREMENT \u003d \"rscp\")\n\nJordan, how do you think we should proceed here? Whatever we do should scale nicely, have reasonable AOSP defaults, and avoid leaking implementation details in CC.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1827,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 1827,
        "endChar": 100
      },
      "revId": "521cd27d622c007a4adf72be7e9e8c6864dbd0c4",
